<title>PERU: Peru's September sugar output up 2.9 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's September sugar output up 2.9 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's sugar production rose 2.9 percent in September to 608,100 tonnes, compared to the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Monday.</p>
<p>The ministry's monthly report added that sugar output for the first nine months was off 4.1 percent to 4.303 million tonnes, compared to the same period last year.</p>
<p>Total 1995 production was 6.325 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Imports of sugar rose 80.1 percent in September to 21,795 tonnes, worth $7.4 million. In the first nine months imports rose 28.4 percent to 235,538 tonnes, worth $79.4 million.</p>
<p>There were no export figures for September.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
